<article class="env-lemma" id="0FZ8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FZ8">Lemma <span data-tag="0FZ8">57.9.9</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a smooth proper scheme over $k$. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $H : D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to \mathcal{A}$ be a homological functor (Derived Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/0147" data-tag="0147">13.3.5</a>) such that for all $K$ in $D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ the object $H^ i(K)$ is nonzero for only a finite number of $i \in \mathbf{Z}$. Then there exists an integer $m \geq 1$ such that $H^ i(\mathcal{F}) = 0$ for any coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{F}$ and $i \not\in [-m, m]$. Similarly for cohomological functors. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemma <a href="/tag/0FZ7" data-tag="0FZ7">57.9.8</a> with Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FX8" data-tag="0FX8">13.35.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>